{"content":[{"c":["GIRGASHITES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Canaanite tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.16","r":"Gen.10.16","rawR":"Gen.10.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.16","value":"Gen.10.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.14","r":"1Chr.1.14","rawR":"1Chr.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.14","value":"1Chr.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:14"},") whose land was promised to Abraham (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.21","r":"Gen.15.21","rawR":"Gen.15.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.21","value":"Gen.15.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 15:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.7.1","r":"Deut.7.1","rawR":"Deut.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.7.1","value":"Deut.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 7:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.10","r":"Josh.3.10","rawR":"Josh.3.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.10","value":"Josh.3.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 3:10"},") and was ultimately acquired (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.24.11","r":"Josh.24.11","rawR":"Josh.24.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.24.11","value":"Josh.24.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 24:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.9.8","r":"Neh.9.8","rawR":"Neh.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.9.8","value":"Neh.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 9:8"},"). The tribe’s location is unknown, though they may have lived in Karkisha, a city mentioned in Hittite texts, or in Kirkishati, an area east of the Tigris. The name ",{"c":["Gresh"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," appeared in 13th century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," Ugaritic texts and might indicate a tribe. In ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.28","r":"Matt.8.28","rawR":"Matt.8.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.28","value":"Matt.8.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matthew 8:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.1","r":"Mark.5.1","rawR":"Mark.5.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.1","value":"Mark.5.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 5:1"},"; and ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.8.26","r":"Luke.8.26","rawR":"Luke.8.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.8.26","value":"Luke.8.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 8:26"},", a name variously translated as “Gergesenes” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), “Gerasenes,” and “Gadarenes” may preserve the tradition of Girgashite occupation of Palestine."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Girgashites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.14","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.14","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.14"},{"anchorText":"Gn 15:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.15.21","rawQueryValue":"Gen.15.21","sourceRefExact":"Gen.15.21"},{"anchorText":"Dt 7:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.7.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.7.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.7.1"},{"anchorText":"Jos 3:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.3.10","rawQueryValue":"Josh.3.10","sourceRefExact":"Josh.3.10"},{"anchorText":"Jos 24:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.24.11","rawQueryValue":"Josh.24.11","sourceRefExact":"Josh.24.11"},{"anchorText":"Neh 9:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.9.8","rawQueryValue":"Neh.9.8","sourceRefExact":"Neh.9.8"},{"anchorText":"Matthew 8:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.8.28","rawQueryValue":"Matt.8.28","sourceRefExact":"Matt.8.28"},{"anchorText":"Mark 5:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.5.1","rawQueryValue":"Mark.5.1","sourceRefExact":"Mark.5.1"},{"anchorText":"Luke 8:26","canonicalization":"deferred_t